{"id":"wikibooks:chili-powder-ii","verdict":"keep","recipes":[{"source":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3AChili_Powder_II","status":"fixed","reason":"Restore nested chile varieties as alternatives, not extra unquantified ingredients.","ingredients":["3–8 dried chilies, mixed to taste: ancho (mild), pasilla (mild), mulato (mild), New Mexico/ristra (medium), cascabel (medium), or chiltepin (very hot)","1 tablespoon cumin seed","1 tablespoon coriander seed","1 tablespoon ground paprika","2 teaspoons whole cloves or allspice","1 teaspoon oregano","1 teaspoon ground red cayenne pepper"],"steps":["Wearing protective gloves, break up the chilies into small pieces, and remove the seeds (or leave the seeds in for a hotter and slightly bitter flavor).","Toast the chilies, cumin, coriander, cloves, and allspice in a dry skillet over low heat, stirring continually until you can smell the peppers (about 2 minutes). Depending on skillet size and pepper quantity, work in batches if necessary.","When the toasted ingredients are cool, transfer them to a food processor or blender with the other ingredients, and grind into a powder. Do not open the lid until the powder settles.","Store in an airtight jar."]}]}
